              "question_type": "PYQ",
              "exam_source": "INI-CET Nov 2023",
              "topic": "Lower Limb Nerve Injuries - Foot Drop",
              "question": "A 26-year-old athlete sustains a direct blow to the lateral aspect of the right knee during a football match. Physical examination demonstrates loss of ankle dorsiflexion, inability to evert the foot, and sensory loss over the dorsum of the foot and first web space. A fracture of which bony landmark is most frequently associated with this presentation?",
