              "question": "A 58-year-old male with small cell lung carcinoma complains of progressive proximal lower limb weakness and dry mouth. On repetitive nerve stimulation at high frequency (20-50 Hz) or following 10 seconds of maximal voluntary contraction, an incremental increase (facilitation >100%) in compound muscle action potential (CMAP) amplitude is noted. Antibodies in this condition are targeted against:",
