              "question": "A 45-year-old female with Graves' disease is administered high doses of potassium iodide (Lugol's solution) prior to undergoing subtotal thyroidectomy. Which acute physiological phenomenon explains the rapid, transient downregulation of thyroid hormone synthesis and glandular vascularity following an acute excess load of inorganic iodide?",
