              "topic": "Glycolysis Regulation - Phosphofructokinase-1",
              "question": "Phosphofructokinase-1 (PFK-1) is the committed rate-limiting enzyme of glycolysis, catalyzing the conversion of fructose-6-phosphate to fructose-1,6-bisphosphate. What is the most potent allosteric activator of PFK-1 that overrides high ATP inhibition during the fed state?",
