              "question_type": "PYQ",
              "exam_source": "INI-CET May 2023",
              "topic": "Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD)",
              "question": "A 5-day-old neonate develops poor feeding, vomiting, hypertonia with alternating episodes of flaccidity, and severe encephalopathy. The infant's diapers possess a distinctive sweet odor resembling burnt sugar or maple syrup. Plasma amino acid chromatography demonstrates elevated levels of branched-chain amino acids. Deficiency of which enzyme complex is present?",
              "options": {
                "A": "Branched-chain alpha-ketoacid dehydrogenase (BCKDH)",
                "B": "Isovaleryl-CoA dehydrogenase",
                "C": "Propionyl-CoA carboxylase",
                "D": "Methylmalonyl-CoA mutase"
              },
              "correct_option": "A",
              "explanation": {
                "rationale": "Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD) is an autosomal recessive deficiency of the mitochondrial branched-chain alpha-ketoacid dehydrogenase complex (BCKDH), which catalyzes the oxidative decarboxylation of alpha-ketoacids derived from the branched-chain amino acids (BCAAs): Leucine, Isoleucine, and Valine. Accumulation of BCAAs (especially neurotoxic Leucine) leads to severe progressive neonatal ketoacidosis, cerebral edema, and the sweet burnt-caramel odor in urine (attributed to isoleucine metabolite). BCKDH requires the cofactor Thiamine (TLCFN).",
                "distractor_analysis": {
                  "A": "Correct. BCKDH deficiency leads to accumulation of Leucine, Isoleucine, and Valine (I Love Vermont maple syrup).",
                  "B": "Isovaleryl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency causes Isovaleric Acidemia (sweaty feet odor).",
                  "C": "Propionyl-CoA carboxylase deficiency causes Propionic Acidemia (biotin requiring).",
                  "D": "Methylmalonyl-CoA mutase deficiency causes Methylmalonic Acidemia (requires vitamin B12)."
                },
                "high_yield_pearl": "Maple Syrup Urine Disease: Block in Branched-Chain Alpha-Ketoacid Dehydrogenase (BCAAs: Leucine, Isoleucine, Valine). Burnt sugar / maple syrup urine odor. Requires 5 cofactors (TLCFN: Thiamine pyrophosphate, Lipoic acid, Coenzyme A, FAD, NAD). Some mild variants respond to high-dose THIAMINE."
              },
