              "question": "A 4-year-old child ingests Datura stramonium seeds and presents with delirium, dilated sluggish pupils, hyperpyrexia, flushed dry skin, and sinus tachycardia of 150 bpm. Which of the following is the specific antidote for reversing BOTH the central and peripheral manifestations?",
