              "topic": "ACE Inhibitors vs ARBs Mechanism & Cough",
              "question": "Why do Angiotensin-Converting Enzyme (ACE) inhibitors cause persistent dry cough and angioedema in up to 10% of patients, whereas Angiotensin Receptor Blockers (ARBs) do not?",
