              "id": "PHARM_Q07_01",
              "exam_source": "NEET PG 2013 Recall",
              "topic": "Antineoplastics - Methotrexate Rescue",
              "question": "A patient with osteosarcoma receives high-dose Methotrexate therapy followed 24 hours later by Leucovorin (folinic acid). What is the biochemical purpose of Leucovorin rescue?",
              "options": {
                "A": "It bypasses the blocked enzyme dihydrofolate reductase to rescue normal host cells from lethal myelosuppression",
                "B": "It accelerates renal tubular excretion of methotrexate",
                "C": "It inhibits xanthine oxidase to prevent hyperuricemia",
                "D": "It cross-links DNA strands in cancer cells synergistically"
              },
              "correct_option": "A",
              "explanation": {
                "rationale": "Methotrexate competitively inhibits Dihydrofolate Reductase (DHFR), preventing the conversion of dihydrofolate to tetrahydrofolate (THF), halting thymidylate and purine synthesis. High-dose methotrexate saturates and kills tumor cells, but also destroys rapidly dividing normal cells (bone marrow and GI mucosa). Leucovorin (folinic acid / 5-formyl-THF) is fully reduced folate that is converted directly into THF derivatives WITHOUT requiring the blocked DHFR enzyme. It selectively rescues healthy host tissues from lethal toxicity.",
                "distractor_analysis": {
                  "B": "Leucovorin does not alter methotrexate clearance; alkalinization with sodium bicarbonate prevents renal crystallization.",
                  "C": "Allopurinol and Rasburicase prevent hyperuricemia.",
                  "D": "Leucovorin is a rescue agent, not a cytotoxic synergy agent."
                },
                "high_yield_pearl": "Methotrexate Antidotes: LEUCOVORIN (Folinic acid) rescues bone marrow. GLUCARPIDASE (carboxypeptidase G2) is an emergency enzyme that cleaves extracellular methotrexate in patients with acute renal failure."
              },
              "tags": [
                "Anticancer",
                "Methotrexate",
                "Leucovorin",
                "DHFR",
                "Rescue",
                "NEET PG 2013"
              ],
