              "topic": "Hodgkin Lymphoma - Reed-Sternberg Cell",
              "image_url": "images/reed_sternberg_cell.svg",
              "question": "A 24-year-old male presents with painless cervical lymphadenopathy, night sweats, and low-grade Pel-Ebstein fever. Lymph node excisional biopsy demonstrates large binucleated giant cells with abundant amphophilic cytoplasm, prominent inclusion-like eosinophilic nucleoli surrounded by a clear halo ('owl-eye' appearance), set within a polymorphic inflammatory background of lymphocytes, plasma cells, and eosinophils. Which immunohistochemical profile confirms the diagnosis of Classical Hodgkin Lymphoma?",
