              "question": "A 7-year-old boy presents with periorbital edema, smoky cola-colored urine, and hypertension 2 weeks after an episode of impetigo. Complement C3 level is markedly depressed. Renal biopsy confirms Post-Streptococcal Glomerulonephritis (PSGN). What pathognomonic ultrastructural feature is visualized on electron microscopy?",
