              "topic": "Mycobacterium tuberculosis - Stain & Diagnostics",
              "question": "A 38-year-old male presents with chronic cough, evening pyrexia, weight loss, and apical cavitary infiltrates on chest radiograph. Sputum smear microscopy following carbol fuchsin staining with heat and 20% sulfuric acid decolourization demonstrates bright red, slender, slightly curved beaded rods against a methylene blue background. What lipid component of the mycobacterial cell wall confers this acid-fast staining property?",
