              "question": "A 5-year-old unimmunized child presents with a low-grade fever, bull-neck cervical lymphadenopathy, and a dirty-grey tough pseudomembrane over the tonsils and posterior pharynx that bleeds profusely upon attempted dislodgement. Smear from the membrane stained with Albert's stain reveals green bacilli arranged in Chinese letter patterns with purple-black granules. These metachromatic (volutin) granules chemically consist of:",
