              "question": "A 9-month-old male infant presents with recurrent bacterial otitis media, sinopulmonary infections, and absent tonsils. Serum shows profound deficiency of ALL immunoglobulin classes (IgG, IgA, IgM) and absent peripheral B cells (CD19/CD20). What gene is mutated?",
              "options": {
                "A": "Bruton Tyrosine Kinase (BTK) gene on the X chromosome",
                "B": "CD40 ligand gene",
                "C": "RAG1/RAG2 genes",
                "D": "Adenosine Deaminase gene"
              },
              "correct_option": "A",
              "explanation": {
                "rationale": "X-linked (Bruton) Agammaglobulinemia: Mutation in BTK prevents pre-B cells from maturing into naive B cells. Boys present after 6 months (maternal IgG wanes) with absent tonsils/germinal centers, zero peripheral B cells, and recurrent encapsulated pyogenic infections.",
                "distractor_analysis": {
                  "A": "CORRECT: X-linked (Bruton) Agammaglobulinemia: Mutation in BTK prevents pre-B cells from maturing into naive B cells. Boys present after 6 months (maternal IgG wanes) with absent tonsils/germinal centers, zero peripheral B cells, and recurrent encapsulated pyogenic infections.",
                  "B": "INCORRECT: CD40 ligand gene is not the primary mechanism, culprit, or first-line choice in this clinical scenario.",
                  "C": "INCORRECT: RAG1/RAG2 genes is not the primary mechanism, culprit, or first-line choice in this clinical scenario.",
                  "D": "INCORRECT: Adenosine Deaminase gene is not the primary mechanism, culprit, or first-line choice in this clinical scenario."
                },
                "high_yield_pearl": "Bruton Agammaglobulinemia (XLA): X-linked recessive defect in BTK (Bruton Tyrosine Kinase). No mature B cells (absent CD19/CD20), all immunoglobulins decreased. Absent tonsils and lymph nodes. Recurrent bacterial and enteroviral infections after 6 months."
              },
