              "topic": "Post-Mortem Lividity - Distinctive Colors",
              "question": "During medicolegal autopsy of a deceased individual recovered from a closed room with a smouldering coal brazier (angithi), bright cherry-pink to cherry-red post-mortem hypostasis (lividity) is noted across dependent areas. This distinctive color of lividity is characteristic of poisoning with:",
