              "question": "A farmer ingests Aluminium Phosphide tablets (Celphos) in a suicide attempt. He presents with severe hypotension, garlic-like odor on breath, refractory metabolic acidosis, and acute pulmonary edema. What lethal gas is liberated in the stomach, and what is the treatment?",
