              "exam_source": "NEET PG 2024",
              "topic": "Bio-Medical Waste Management Rules 2016",
              "image_url": "images/bmw_color_bins.svg",
              "question": "According to the Bio-Medical Waste Management (Amendment) Rules 2016 and 2018 in India, in which color-coded category container should contaminated, recyclable plastic wastes such as used intravenous infusion tubing, Foley catheters, urine bags, and disposable latex gloves be segregated?",
              "options": {
                "A": "Red non-chlorinated plastic bag / container",
                "B": "Yellow non-chlorinated plastic bag",
                "C": "White translucent, puncture-proof, tamper-proof container",
                "D": "Blue cardboard box with blue marking"
              },
              "correct_option": "A",
              "explanation": {
                "rationale": "Under the Bio-Medical Waste Management Rules 2016 (Government of India): 1. RED CATEGORY: Contaminated recyclable plastics (tubings, IV sets, catheters, urine bags, disposable gloves, vacutainers) undergo autoclaving/microwaving followed by shredding and recycling. 2. YELLOW CATEGORY: Human anatomical waste, animal tissue, soiled cotton/dressings, expired/discarded cytotoxic drugs, and body fluid-contaminated linen (treated by incineration or plasma pyrolysis). 3. WHITE (Translucent): Needles, scalpel blades, fixed needles (puncture-proof, autoclave + shredding). 4. BLUE: Broken glassware, medicine vials, ampoules, and orthopedic implants (disinfection with sodium hypochlorite or autoclaving).",
                "distractor_analysis": {
                  "A": "Correct. Red container is designated strictly for contaminated recyclable plastic waste (Tubing, Catheters, Gloves).",
                  "B": "Yellow is designated for human anatomical waste, soiled dressings, and cytotoxic drugs for incineration.",
                  "C": "White translucent is for metallic sharps and blades.",
                  "D": "Blue is for glassware (ampoules, vials) and metallic implants."
                },
                "high_yield_pearl": "Bio-Medical Waste Mnemonic: RED = Recyclable Plastics (Rubber, Tubing, Catheters). YELLOW = Anatomical & Soiled dressings & Cytotoxic (Incineration). WHITE = Sharps (Needles, Scalpels). BLUE = Broken Glass & Implants (Vials, Ampoules)."
              },
