              "question": "A 3-year-old malnourished child is brought with inability to see in dim light at dusk (Nyctalopia). Slit-lamp examination reveals triangular, dry, silvery-foamy plaques on the temporal bulbar conjunctiva. What are these spots and what WHO stage do they represent?",
