                "rationale": "With-the-rule (WTR) astigmatism is the commonest physiological form in young individuals, where the vertical corneal curvature is steeper (greater dioptric power) than horizontal. It is corrected by concave cylinder at 180 degrees or convex cylinder at 90 degrees. Against-the-rule (ATR) is common in elderly (horizontal steeper). Irregular astigmatism requires rigid gas-permeable contact lenses.",
