              "question": "A 48-year-old executive complains of slowly progressive hearing loss in his left ear and difficulty understanding speech on his mobile phone for 2 years. Audiometry reveals high-frequency sensorineural hearing loss with speech discrimination score disproportionately worse than pure-tone thresholds. Corneal reflex is diminished on the left. What is the gold-standard imaging modality?",
