              "question": "A 28-year-old male develops complete unilateral lower motor neuron facial paralysis after a skull base fracture. Topodiagnostic testing demonstrates absent lacrimation on Schirmer's test, absent stapedial acoustic reflex, and loss of taste on the anterior two-thirds of the tongue. At or proximal to what anatomical ganglion is the facial nerve injured?",
