                "high_yield_pearl": "Facial Nerve Topodiagnosis: Proximal to Geniculate Ganglion: Decreased lacrimation (Schirmer test abnormal) + Absent stapedial reflex + Loss of taste (chorda tympani). Between Geniculate and N. to Stapedius: Normal lacrimation + Absent stapedial reflex (hyperacusis) + Loss of taste. At Stylomastoid Foramen: Only pure facial motor weakness (lacrimation, hearing, taste all preserved)."
