              "topic": "Neuromuscular Junction - Myasthenia Gravis",
              "question": "A 28-year-old female presents with fluctuating drooping of both eyelids (ptosis) and double vision (diplopia) that worsens significantly toward the end of the day or after prolonged reading. She has mild bilateral facial weakness and fatigable arm abduction weakness after repeated resistance testing, but normal sensory examination and preserved deep tendon reflexes. Autoantibodies against which of the following structures are the pathophysiological cause of her illness?",
