                "rationale": "The classic presentation of fluctuating, fatigable weakness of ocular and bulbar muscles that worsens with repetitive exertion and improves with rest is the hallmark of MYASTHENIA GRAVIS. In ~85% of generalized cases, circulating autoantibodies directed against postsynaptic nicotinic acetylcholine receptors (AChR) on the motor endplate cause complement-mediated receptor destruction, functional receptor blockade, and receptor cross-linking/internalization. In AChR-negative patients, anti-MuSK (muscle-specific kinase) or anti-LRP4 antibodies are found.",
