                "rationale": "Brown-Sequard syndrome (spinal cord hemisection): (1) Lateral Corticospinal Tract crosses in the medulla: hemisection causes IPSILATERAL Upper Motor Neuron spastic paralysis below the lesion. (2) Dorsal Columns (Gracile/Cuneate) ascend uncrossed until the medulla: hemisection causes IPSILATERAL loss of vibration, joint position sense, and discriminative touch below the lesion. (3) Spinothalamic Tract decussates within 1 to 2 spinal segments: hemisection causes CONTRALATERAL loss of pain and temperature sensation beginning 1-2 segments below the lesion. At the level of the lesion: ipsilateral lower motor neuron flaccidity and total anesthesia.",
