              "topic": "Portal Hypertension - Variceal Bleeding",
              "question": "A 46-year-old male with chronic alcoholic liver cirrhosis presents with acute onset of vomiting 800 mL of bright red blood (hematemesis). Vitals: BP 80/50 mmHg, HR 122 bpm. Physical exam shows jaundice, bilateral palmar erythema, shifting dullness, and caput medusae around the umbilicus. After airway stabilization and initiation of crystalloid resuscitation and blood transfusion, which of the following represents the most appropriate immediate medical and endoscopic management combination?",
