              "question": "A 52-year-old female presents with progressive abdominal distension for 3 months. Diagnostic paracentesis is performed, and laboratory analysis demonstrates:\n• Serum Albumin: 3.6 g/dL\n• Ascitic Fluid Albumin: 1.8 g/dL\n• Ascitic Total Protein: 1.2 g/dL\nWhat is the Serum-Ascites Albumin Gradient (SAAG) and the most likely pathological category of ascites?",
