                "high_yield_pearl": "SAAG Classification Guide:\n• High SAAG (>= 1.1 g/dL) -> PORTAL HYPERTENSION PRESENT:\n  - Low ascitic protein (< 2.5 g/dL): Cirrhosis, Late Budd-Chiari.\n  - High ascitic protein (>= 2.5 g/dL): Cardiac ascites (Heart failure, Constrictive pericarditis), Early Budd-Chiari.\n• Low SAAG (< 1.1 g/dL) -> NO PORTAL HYPERTENSION (Peritoneal pathology):\n  - Peritoneal Carcinomatosis, Tuberculous Peritonitis, Nephrotic Syndrome, Pancreatic ascites."
