              "question": "A 30-year-old female taking oral contraceptive pills presents with sudden acute right upper quadrant abdominal pain, rapid development of tense ascites, and painful tender hepatomegaly. Hepatic Doppler ultrasound demonstrates absent flow in the hepatic veins with hypertrophy of the caudate lobe. What is the diagnosis, and why does the caudate lobe undergo compensatory hypertrophy?",
