                "high_yield_pearl": "SIADH Rules: Euvolemic hypotonic hyponatremia + Inappropriately concentrated urine (Uosm > 100) + High urine sodium (> 20 mEq/L). Causes: Small cell lung cancer (ectopic ADH), SSRIs, Carbamazepine, CNS infections. Treatment: Fluid restriction (DOC). Vasopressin V2 antagonists (Tolvaptan / Conivaptan). Golden Safety Rule: Correct slowly (< 8-10 mEq/L in 24 hours) to prevent Central Pontine Myelinolysis (Osmotic Demyelination Syndrome)! 'From Low to High, Your Pons Will Die; From High to Low, Your Brain Will Blow' (cerebral edema)."
