                  "D": "Bartter syndrome is an autosomal recessive loop-diuretic-like tubulopathy (NKCC2 mutation); it presents with hypokalemic metabolic alkalosis, but with NORMAL or LOW blood pressure and HIGH renin/aldosterone."
