              "question": "A 36-year-old male presents with acute, severe, spasmodic right flank pain radiating to the groin (ureteral colic) and microscopic hematuria. Non-contrast CT of the abdomen confirms a 4 mm stone at the right vesicoureteral junction. What is the most common mineral composition of kidney stones worldwide, and which stone is radiolucent on plain abdominal radiographs?",
