              "question": "A 62-year-old male receives unfractionated heparin for DVT prophylaxis following hip replacement. On postoperative day 7, his platelet count drops by 55% from 280,000 to 125,000/uL, and he develops acute pain and swelling in his right arm around a peripheral venous catheter (new venous thrombosis). What immunological mechanism causes HIT Type 2, and what is the mandatory immediate management?",
