              "topic": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) & BCR-ABL",
              "question": "A 48-year-old male presents with massive splenomegaly extending 10 cm below the left costal margin, fatigue, and early satiety. Complete blood count shows marked leukocytosis (WBC 168,000/uL) with the full spectrum of granulocytic differentiation from blasts to mature neutrophils, and prominent basophilia (4%). Leukocyte Alkaline Phosphatase (LAP / NAP) score is markedly LOW at 8 (normal 40-100). What cytogenetic translocation generates the Philadelphia Chromosome, and what is the first-line targeted therapy?",
